+PATCHED 15.1 — 05/10/2026
+- Real test by the user (05/10/2026 12:59, Comment mode, post with 733
+  comments): the comment list loaded (47 commenters) and the FIRST
+  web_profile_info request got HTTP 429 without Retry-After. The extension
+  paused until 13:59:23, marked the row as an access failure and repeated
+  nothing. The public commercial email is still not confirmed.
+- The Comment progress line counted checked profiles as "perfis encontrados"
+  and showed "0" while 47 commenters were listed. It now reads
+  "47 perfis encontrados, 0 consultados".
+- The popup shows the full patch level (e.g. "PATCHED 15.1").
+
+PATCHED 15 — 05/10/2026
+Stability release for every mode. The Comment-mode route and its limits are
+unchanged from PATCHED 14: one ordinary web_profile_info request per profile,
+serial, 10 s minimum spacing, shared persistent 429 cooldown (Retry-After,
+60 min default), no automatic retry, no /users/{id}/info/ in Comment mode.
+A public commercial email delivered by that route is still NOT confirmed by a
+real response: no request to Instagram was possible while building it.
+
+Fixes
+- Comment resume: the history counted listed commenters as extracted, so a
+  resume after a 429 skipped commenters never checked (98 of 150 in the
+  simulation; all of them when the 429 came on the first check). Counts now
+  use checked profiles only, the end of the comment list no longer marks the
+  history as complete, and a resume skips exactly the profiles already
+  stored. Counters saved by older versions are not trusted for Comment mode.
+- History rows: one row per profile (no duplicates after a resume). Rows saved
+  by older versions are cleaned on resume, so a bio/site email never fills the
+  email column again. The popup History export applies the same rule, uses
+  the "E-mail comercial" header plus the "Status do e-mail" column, and its
+  email count matches what it exports.
+- DJ filter: it filters the table and the export only. It no longer decides
+  which rows are saved, when a run completes or the history counters (with
+  the filter on, a run never completed and hidden rows vanished from History).
+- Other modes, deleted profile: a 404 on the profile detail is recorded as
+  "Perfil indisponível" and the queue moves on. Before, it was retried, opened
+  an instagram.com tab and the run never completed. Three in a row pause the
+  run for a session check, without automatic retry.
+- Other modes, errors: a failing profile is retried once, then recorded as a
+  failure in the status column so the run can complete. The retry counter now
+  resets after every answered profile (two errors anywhere in a run used to
+  disable every later retry). A login/HTML page keeps that profile as the next
+  one to try.
+- Other modes, renamed profile: the detail is matched by id, so a profile
+  renamed between the list and its detail keeps its commercial email.
+- User list: a name with no profile is recorded as unavailable and never
+  produces a /users//info/ request with an empty id; network errors stay
+  retryable on resume; an empty or already finished list completes.
+- Background instagram.com "claim" tab: once per 100 processed profiles. In
+  Comment mode with 100, 200, ... commenters it opened on every profile.
+- Saved 429 pause: the other modes resume by themselves when a pause saved by
+  another dashboard ends (Comment mode still waits for Iniciar).
+- History index: saves from two open dashboards no longer overwrite each
+  other's entries and dates (the 190-day cleanup could delete a history that
+  had just been used).
+- Instagram's own error text is stripped of markup in every notification.
+
+Validation: 41 parser/reader unit tests; 12 data/history tests that run the
+real dashboard and popup code in Node (10 of them fail on PATCHED 14, which
+reproduces the defects above); end-to-end runs of the real dashboard in
+Chromium for every mode. Every Instagram response in these tests is simulated.
+
+==============================================================================
